    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Crescent Lake is a picturesque community nestled in the heart of the stunning Cascade Range.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.southernoregon.org/cities/crescent-lake/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community of Crescent Lake was originally built to service steam trains and maintain tracks along the Southern Pacific Railroad line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crescent_Lake%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Crescent Lake once served as a division meeting point where freight train crews from Eugene and Klamath Falls relieved each other.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crescent_Lake%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original site featured a train depot, a roundhouse, a one-room schoolhouse, and a lodging facility known as the Clubhouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crescent_Lake%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Crescent Lake began moving to its present site along Oregon Route 58 after World War II.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
